{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The analysis has identified several instances where the draft application introduces technical details, optional embodiments, and methods of use that are not supported by the affirmative statements in the inventor's source documents.\n\nSpecifically, the draft speculates on the precise geometry and method for using the alignment sights, introduces a new functional purpose for the replaceable drill bushings (changing hole size) that the inventor did not disclose, adds speculative shapes for the pointers, and describes a specific multi-workpiece method that is not in the source. Each of these additions constitutes an unsupported assertion of invention detail.\n\nThe following findings detail each discrepancy and provide a corrective action to remove the unsupported language, ensuring the final application is faithful to the inventor's disclosure. No issues of internal consistency or formatting were found. The figure briefs were found to use acceptable depiction conventions for generic shapes without adding unsupported technical substance."}
