{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the patent application drafts. The review compared the claims, description, and figures against the authoritative source documents provided by the inventor.\n\nThe review found four instances of critical `disclosure_fidelity` issues where the draft application introduces specific geometric, functional, or optional features that are not explicitly described or supported by the inventor's disclosure. These include unsupported geometric limitations for the sight notch and clamping shoe, and an unsupported function and embodiment related to replacing drill bushings to change hole diameters. The inventor's disclosure only supports replacing bushings due to wear.\n\nEach finding includes a detailed explanation, evidence from both the draft and source texts, and a specific, actionable fix to bring the application into compliance with the source material. No other issues related to internal consistency, terminology, or formalities were found.\n\nI will now submit the detailed findings."}
